Article 17: Before the auction commences, the People's Court shall withdraw the auction commission under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The effective legal instrument on the basis of which enforcement is carried out has been revoked;
(2) The applicant for enforcement and other enforcement creditors withdraw the enforcement application;
(3) The person subjected to enforcement has fully performed the monetary obligations determined by the legal instrument;
(4) The parties have reached a settlement agreement in enforcement and the auction of the property is unnecessary;
(5) A person other than a party raises a well-founded objection to the auctioned property;
(6) The auction institution and bidders maliciously collude;
(7) Other circumstances in which the auction commission shall be withdrawn.
